{"author":{"id":"78f9c13831d7e4cd23da41f1921a0df29d82a91276573361524e3bf648269089"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1787147760,"nonce":"xBYSh7twE58KuQZL5JEuEC3aEYA=","metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lAHOOEv6_s8AAAABNY0rr87e9gJ8"},"target":"c6353bfb7d2d11db7b7e75e9301c6a743bc6c03ba4cbe87ea45ca6d5f844b946","message":"The underlying issue is [RUSTSEC-2026-0258](https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0258), and due to our dependency on rocket, as reported by cargo-deny:\n\n```\n  │ error[vulnerability]: h2 unbounded empty DATA frames\n  │     ┌─ /Volumes/scratch/repos/gwr/Cargo.lock:120:1\n  │     │\n  │ 120 │ h2 0.3.27 registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index\n  │     │ ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━ security vulnerability detected\n  │     │\n  │     ├ ID: RUSTSEC-2026-0258\n  │     ├ Advisory: https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0258\n  │     ├ The h2 crate, used internally by hyper, had a flaw that would accept and queue empty DATA frames without limit.\n  │       If streams were not actively drained, this could lead to unbounded memory usage, or a panic if the length overflows.\n  │       \n  │       Low severity.\n  │       \n  │       Patched in v0.4.16.\n  │     ├ Announcement: https://github.com/hyperium/hyper/security/advisories/GHSA-q83h-524g-xf6h\n  │     ├ Solution: Upgrade to \u003e=0.4.16 (try `cargo update -p h2`)\n  │     ├ h2 v0.3.27\n  │       └── hyper v0.14.32\n  │           └── rocket_http v0.5.1\n  │               ├── rocket v0.5.1\n  │               │   └── gwr-spotter v0.9.0\n  │               └── rocket_codegen v0.5.1\n  │                   └── rocket v0.5.1 (*)\n```\n\nThe rocket project appears to have stalled, with no current commit activity or recent releases. It depends on a version of hyper which cargo cannot simply update to allow us to pickup a fixed release of h2.\n\nThe Rust community appears to have moved to generally recommending [axum](https://crates.io/crates/axum) rather than rocket, which is part of and maintained by the Tokio project.\n\naxum also depends on hyper, though it uses a recent release which itself is compatible with versions of h2 that do not suffer from the vulnerability. \n\nThis issue is currently blocking pull requests from landing as cargo-deny will cause the lint job to fail.","files":null},{"type":5,"timestamp":1787147653,"nonce":"9BlSGsr/aOgUqXkx0B4nb8PMPUY=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOOEv6_s8AAAABNY0rr88AAAAG6W03Dw"},"added":["C - bug"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"timestamp":1787147653,"nonce":"3TJwZNHD3yR4zON6Hbq8a8yPzH8=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOOEv6_s8AAAABNY0rr88AAAAG6W03yA"},"added":["A - track"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"timestamp":1787147654,"nonce":"LwFXg9Q7xN0+YfjZD1UiAtCGhBM=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOOEv6_s8AAAABNY0rr88AAAAG6W04eQ"},"added":["C - cleanup"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"timestamp":1787147654,"nonce":"2OXvnP5QDpm1fKyezhTiLloyRR0=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOOEv6_s8AAAABNY0rr88AAAAG6W05Xg"},"added":["A - visualisation"],"removed":[]}]}